# The only ignore file this repo maintains. A nested one outranks it: git
# resolves by depth, which is how a vendored crate's own rules once hid its
# `Cargo.lock` from `git add` while `scripts/vendor.py` was still hashing it.
# `publish` strips them from generated trees; CI rejects any other.
# `.claude/skills` is a symlink, so nothing under it is ours to ignore.

# Rust. `**/` because cargo also runs in `fuzz/` and in a vendored crate
# someone is debugging a patch against.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# `Cargo.lock` is deliberately absent: this crate is a binary's core, and every
# vendored crate ships one. Ignoring it broke the vendor subsystem once.

# cargo-fuzz. Reproducible from a run, none of it history.
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/coverage/

# CPython writes a cache beside any module it imports, and `scripts/vendor.py`
# imports itself for its doctests.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/

# Per-developer noise. Anything genuinely shared comes back by negation here.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
